{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475216-v5-london-chronicle-modern-nights","id":1475216,"title":"V5 London Chronicle (Modern Nights)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-22T03:29:03-08:00","id":1475216,"title":"V5 London Chronicle (Modern Nights)","content":"TL;DR - Looking for ideas for a modern-nights London chronicle. <hr /><br /> I'm looking at taking my second shot at running a Chronicle in London. My group is a mix of Camarilla and Hecata members who're looking to restore the city to Camarilla rule after the purge at the hands of Operation: Antigen.<br /> <br /> <b>Wondering what sorts of things everyone would expect to see in a London based chronicle? I've currently got ideas for:</b><br /> - Camarilla retaking the city: Lady Scarlett, Valerius, &amp; a Mithraist competing for Praxis.<br /> - Operation-Antigen: The Second Inquisition are still attacking the Kindred of London and need to be dealt with.<br /> - Sabbat &amp; Anarch Remnants: Both groups are still trying to salvage what they can from the city and are opposed to anything the Camarilla may attempt to achieve.<br /> <br /> <b>Any ideas for:</b><br /> - Locations<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">- Rundown industrial or urban centres would be interesting.<br /> - Occult spaces or locations.<br /> - Interesting underground locations.</div> - NPC's<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">- Canon NPC's (I've got Fall of London and the Victorian London book)<br /> - Ideas for interesting London based NPC's</div> - Plot-Hooks<br /> - Inspiration (Be very interested in any, Criminal Underworld, Noire or Punk styled stories set in London.)<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">- Books<br /> - Comics<br /> - Films, etc. </div> <hr /><br /> <b>My current coterie is looking like:</b><br /> <b>1) Evie Knight - Banu-Haqim, Alastor:</b> Hoping to assist the Camarilla in establishing Praxis, whilst also hunting down her former mentor now potential Red-Lister, the Ventrue mob boss Owen Marks.<br /> <br /> <b>2) Mira - Telyavelic Tremere, Occult-Survivor:</b> Looking to find her place in the Camarilla after her sire was killed. Keen to discover what happened to her sire if she can. (Possibly getting drawn into the Bahari.)<br /> <br /> <b>3) Giorgio Giovanni - Giovanni, Blackmailer &amp; Fixer:</b> Looking to further the family's interests in London by supporting a weakened Camarilla in need of all the support it can get. (Personal aspirations to become the Hecata Boss of London.)<br /> <br /> <b>4) XXX - Thin-Blood, Dealer &amp; Alchemist:</b> Looking to escape Owen Marks and his criminal associates, whilst finding a way to survive in whatever the future of London may hold. They're keen to make amends for the damage done as a dealer and working for Owen Marks.<br /> <br /> <b>5) XXX - Brujah/Gangrel, Enforcer/New Media Influencer: </b>Don't have much information on this one, other than they'll probably have good physicals or lots of contacts in the press and proficiency in tech.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STV Author - <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/374164/Guide-to-the-Sabbat?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=0_0_45624_0_0_0_0\" target=\"_blank\">Guide to the Sabbat</a> <br /> Current Project(s): Tales from the Fronts - A Guide to the Gehenna War","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25061-karos","name":"Karos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25061_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T06:02:50-08:00","id":1475227,"title":"","content":"Neither book's is quite in the modern era, but <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Giovanni_Chronicles_II:_Blood_%26_Fire\" target=\"_blank\">Blood &amp; Fire</a>, at least partly set in 1666 London and <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Giovanni_Chronicles_III:_The_Sun_Has_Set\" target=\"_blank\">its sequel</a>, that occurs, at least in part, the same city in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Revolutions_of_1848\" target=\"_blank\">1848</a>, might be of potential interest for elder &amp; ancilla NPCs (Giovanni and otherwise) to mine, among other things perhaps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-22-2022, 09:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T06:13:55-08:00","id":1475230,"title":"","content":"London has a pretty dope underground: Abandoned railway lines, bunkers, a pretty extensive sewer system. The thing is that London is too big. It'd work better as a group of princedoms (or a complicated feudal structure) so I'd prefer to focus on a region rather than use the whole city. IE Your vampires hold court in Islington or Camden or Chiswick rather than Westminster. <br /> <br /> <br /> London is a very rapidly changing city especially in terms of demographics. If you use sources from anything more than 10 years ago you'll get a very different city from the reality. In 1991, london was 80% white, in 2011, 60% white: with less than 45% of the population identified as &quot;white-British&quot;. As Vampires largely focus on the denser inner city, this change is much more pronounced. So a lot of good shows from/set 30+ years ago are really poor sources for how London is now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T08:15:44-08:00","id":1475235,"title":"","content":"There are some undergrounds that never served any trains, or closed of stations. Like Brittish Museum station.<br /> <br /> Watch or read Neverwhere by Neil Gaiman. Not vampireish but lots of cool stuff about a mysterious London.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25995-ethryo","name":"Ethryo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-24T00:57:58-08:00","id":1475397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475216-v5-london-chronicle-modern-nights?p=1475227#post1475227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neither book's is quite in the modern era, but <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Giovanni_Chronicles_II:_Blood_%26_Fire\" target=\"_blank\">Blood &amp; Fire</a>, at least partly set in 1666 London and <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Giovanni_Chronicles_III:_The_Sun_Has_Set\" target=\"_blank\">its sequel</a>, that occurs, at least in part, the same city in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Revolutions_of_1848\" target=\"_blank\">1848</a>, might be of potential interest for elder &amp; ancilla NPCs (Giovanni and otherwise) to mine, among other things perhaps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the recommendation, I'll be sure to check those out. The mention of Sabbat insurrections in London and questing for the Sargon fragment is particularly intriguing. Be interesting to work in themes of an 1848 insurrection into the modern strains of the Anarch movement. Tie-ins with established Giovanni could also be interesting to explore.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ethryo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475216-v5-london-chronicle-modern-nights?p=1475235#post1475235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Watch or read Neverwhere by Neil Gaiman. Not vampireish but lots of cool stuff about a mysterious London.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the reading recommendation, will have to give it a look-in, see if the local library has a copy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475216-v5-london-chronicle-modern-nights?p=1475230#post1475230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">London has a pretty dope underground: Abandoned railway lines, bunkers, a pretty extensive sewer system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I've started looking into them for some suitable locations. They featured in some of the stronger arcs of my last Chronicle. Especially when the Tremere went delving into the Nosferatu's hidden warrens. Any particular places you can recall?<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ethryo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475216-v5-london-chronicle-modern-nights?p=1475235#post1475235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are some undergrounds that never served any trains, or closed of stations. Like Brittish Museum station.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are certainly some good places to start, stations make for good havens and throughways. Even for mortal criminals and urban explorers, I've got a few friends in that community that might help.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475216-v5-london-chronicle-modern-nights?p=1475230#post1475230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is that London is too big. It'd work better as a group of princedoms (or a complicated feudal structure) so I'd prefer to focus on a region rather than use the whole city. IE Your vampires hold court in Islington or Camden or Chiswick rather than Westminster.</div> </div> </div> </div>My current way of working is to have different Kindred claiming either Boroughs or portions of them, as Landlords. Since the purge by Operation: Antigen, there aren't many Kindred floating around or many safe domains for them to live in. (It helps that even slightly overt fighting for territory is basically suicide with Antigen around.)<br /> <br /> Over the Chronicle though that will change. The PC's can start rallying the various small territories to whichever banner they choose (likely the Camarilla, since that's who they're starting with). They can also weaken the grip of Antigen, removing backers, breaking off component parts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475216-v5-london-chronicle-modern-nights?p=1475230#post1475230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">London is a very rapidly changing city especially in terms of demographics. If you use sources from anything more than 10 years ago you'll get a very different city from the reality. In 1991, london was 80% white, in 2011, 60% white: with less than 45% of the population identified as &quot;white-British&quot;. As Vampires largely focus on the denser inner city, this change is much more pronounced. So a lot of good shows from/set 30+ years ago are really poor sources for how London is now.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one thing I will admit to being worried about, the group playing isn't very diverse (a byproduct of where we live). I try and depict a diverse London, including people of varying cultures and ethnicities. The portrayal is the tricky bit though, getting cultural nuances in particular without them feeling like parodies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STV Author - <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/374164/Guide-to-the-Sabbat?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=0_0_45624_0_0_0_0\" target=\"_blank\">Guide to the Sabbat</a> <br /> Current Project(s): Tales from the Fronts - A Guide to the Gehenna War","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25061-karos","name":"Karos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25061_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-24T06:41:18-08:00","id":1475404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475216-v5-london-chronicle-modern-nights?p=1475397#post1475397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for the recommendation, I'll be sure to check those out. The mention of Sabbat insurrections in London and questing for the Sargon fragment is particularly intriguing. Be interesting to work in themes of an 1848 insurrection into the modern strains of the Anarch movement. Tie-ins with established Giovanni could also be interesting to explore.<br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Truth be told, i think Doctor Streck as described in the Sun Has Set works much better as Anarch than Sabbat.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh, i almost forgot - the Sabbat figure and Anathema <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Dylan_Bruce\" target=\"_blank\">Dylan Bruce</a>, from <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/The_Kindred_Most_Wanted_(book)\" target=\"_blank\">Kindred Most Wanted</a> and <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Dread_Names,_Red_List\" target=\"_blank\">Dread Names, Red List</a>, was embraced in London, though i'm not sure how much of a local he might or not still be considered (what doesn't stop one of making a cameo or story arc with him). Also of note <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Gotsdam\" target=\"_blank\">his sire</a>, who also makes an appearance in Beckett's Jyhad Diary, probably the most powerful kindred of the British Isles outside of Mithras or Kemintiri (ok, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Tiamat_(VTM)\" target=\"_blank\">with one notable exception</a>).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-24-2022, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-24T07:09:54-08:00","id":1475405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475216-v5-london-chronicle-modern-nights?p=1475397#post1475397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's one thing I will admit to being worried about, the group playing isn't very diverse (a byproduct of where we live). I try and depict a diverse London, including people of varying cultures and ethnicities. The portrayal is the tricky bit though, getting cultural nuances in particular without them feeling like parodies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's very possible to overstate the diversity. A lot from these groups are second or third gen immigrants that've assimilated and view themselves as British. A cockney or near cockney accent can come from some surprising faces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}